The `setdiff` function is also an excellent choice for finding the unique elements between two arrays, such as the words in `words1` that are not present in `words2`.

To make this solution even more efficient, you can preallocate the memory for the arrays `words1` and `words2` before reading the text files using the `zeros` function with the appropriate size based on the expected number of words in each text. This will improve the performance when dealing with very large texts.

